      "notes": "Population pharmacokinetic parameters of VOR in rats (autoinduction model)\nS06 | DOI 10.1128/AAC.01556-08 | Table 2 (van de Sande et al. 2009)\nNeutropenic female RP strain albino rats (age and weight not reported); PK groups of 9 uninfected neutropenic rats. Vfend INTRAPERITONEAL q12h for 10 days in four regimens: 2.6 mg/kg; 5 mg/kg; 6, 8, 10, 11 mg/kg on days 1-4 then 12 mg/kg; 7.5, 10, 12.5, 15 mg/kg on days 1-4 then 17.5 mg/kg. Sampling days 0, 5 and 9, three times per rat (0, 2, 8 h; 0.5, 4, 10 h; 1, 6, 12 h); retro-orbital plasma; agar-diffusion bioassay (C. albicans), standards 0.125-4 µg/ml; binding not measured.\nNONMEM model with Michaelis-Menten elimination and enzyme autoinduction: \"the amount of enzyme is increased sixfold on the last day, producing a comparable increase in the Vmax.\" Footnote a: \"Standard errors of the estimates were <42%.\" V in ml and Vmax in μg/h are per animal.\nMeasured concentrations are in Fig. 1 only (days 0 and 9 at 7.5 and 17.5 mg/kg; not digitized; legend does not say whether dots are individual rats).",
      "column_map": {
        "c001_parameter": "Parameter",
        "c002_mean": "Mean",
